{"nodes": [{"id": "forge_readme_forge_app", "label": "The Forge app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registered, deployed to development, reading a real tenant's data; the second of two Jira routes beside OAuth 3LO which needs no app registration. Exists so choosing Forge is a decision rather than a rewrite."}, {"id": "forge_readme_four_files", "label": "The four Forge files", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "manifest.yml (modules, resources, scopes, egress); src/index.js (resolvers, talks to Jira, calls the calculator, computes nothing); src/jira.js (pure shaping, no SDK, so tests can run it); bridge/bridge.js (the transport adapter)."}, {"id": "forge_readme_bridge_seam", "label": "bridge.js is the seam", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "src/app.js is the shipped product and must not learn what Forge is; the page looks for a transport on window.__DVD_BRIDGE__ and the adapter is bundled as a classic script (a module is deferred and would arrive after the page decided it was offline), linked only into the split build."}, {"id": "forge_readme_tools_are_pure_functions", "label": "The functionality is not the problem", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tools are already pure functions (every open() is inside main()); a call is 16 KB and does not grow with the customer; no issue title has to leave Atlassian because forecast.build over dates and status categories is byte-identical, with summaries re-attached by key."}, {"id": "forge_readme_cost_of_the_route", "label": "What the Forge route costs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs on Atlassian badge forfeited to egress; Marketplace review reads the egress declaration; data residency becomes yours per region; you run a stateless service."}, {"id": "forge_readme_story_points_field_discovery", "label": "Story points discovered by display name", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read from whichever field the site calls them via /rest/api/3/field, same three names and first-match traversal as the fetcher, because two producers picking different fields report two velocities. A site with no field reports null, not 0."}, {"id": "forge_readme_app_id_not_committed", "label": "The app id is stripped before commit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "forge register writes an id that ties the manifest to one Atlassian account; strip it before git add, restore after."}, {"id": "forge_readme_forge_static_build", "label": "make forge-static builds the split dashboard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a copy of dist/: the iframe CSP blocks inline style and script so build.py --split links them; seeded from seed.json rather than the demo dataset; --bridge links the adapter ahead of app.js."}, {"id": "forge_src_index", "label": "forge/src/index.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, 